-- title:
--   From HTo G G Hat Idx Meas Sum Is Some True
-- statement:
--   **Nonfailure G-hat outcomes sum to the complete slice mass.** Let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family and fix $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$. Write $U_{x,g}$ for the effect of the indexed G-hat measurement and $C_x$ for the total of `completePartSubMeas`. Summing the outcomes with `isSome = true` gives
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{g\,:\,g.\mathrm{isSome}=\mathrm{true}}U_{x,g}=C_x.
--   $$
--
--   Thus the nonfailure branch is exactly the complete polynomial part before recurrence weights are inserted.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_gHatIdxMeas_sum_isSome_true`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
